Local review patch: stop T6032 DVFS setup after a cluster failure
Base: reviewed m1n1 2460b604c6f016956ead711823605eea840c602e.
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

Stop before programming any later T6032 cluster when initialization fails.
Other SoCs retain the existing best-effort loop and aggregate return status.
This is failure containment, not rollback of earlier register writes or proof
that the selected raw boot states and feature sequence are hardware-safe.

--- a/src/cpufreq.c
+++ b/src/cpufreq.c
@@ -532,6 +532,9 @@
     bool err = false;
     while (cluster->base) {
-        err |= cpufreq_init_cluster(cluster++, features);
+        int status = cpufreq_init_cluster(cluster++, features);
+        if (chip_id == T6032 && status < 0)
+            return status;
+        err |= status;
     }
 
     return err ? -1 : 0;
